  vignette: "A 53-year-old is having a lithium disilicate crown on 3.6 tried in. It stops about 0.5 mm short of the margin, and it feels high. Floss will not pass through the mesial contact, and the internal surface has no visible nodules. Which of the following is the most appropriate first step?",
